.TH QFW-SLURM-BURST-BUFFER.CONF 5 "September 2026" "qfw-slurm 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
qfw-slurm-burst-buffer.conf \- qfw-slurm Lua lifecycle configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/qfw-slurm/burst-buffer.lua.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
This root-owned Lua file returns a table used by
.IR burst_buffer.lua .
It must not be writable by allocation users.
.SH FIELDS
.TP
.BI cluster = "name"
Set the authoritative Slurm cluster name used when teardown must recover a
reservation whose local state file is missing.
.TP
.BI helper = "path"
Set the absolute path to the private
.BR qfw-slurm-bb (8)
helper.
.TP
.BI driver = "path"
Set the absolute path to
.BR qfw-slurm-driver (1).
.TP
.BI plugin_config = "path"
Set the protected native gateway configuration.
.TP
.BI state_dir = "path"
Set the SlurmUser-owned directory containing allocation JSON and environment
records. Compute-node slurmstepd processes must see the same path when the
SPANK module injects application context.
.TP
.BI max_reservation_attempts = count
Set the positive maximum number of final reservation attempts. Exhaustion is
terminal and cancels the job.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
return {
        cluster = "qfw-cluster",
        helper = "/usr/libexec/qfw-slurm/qfw-slurm-bb",
        driver = "/usr/bin/qfw-slurm-driver",
        plugin_config = "/etc/qfw-slurm/plugin.conf",
        state_dir = "/var/lib/qfw-slurm/allocations",
        max_reservation_attempts = 8,
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-slurm-plugin.conf (5),
.BR qfw-slurm (7),
.BR qfw-slurm-bb (8)
